This is a classic issue when switching APIs. You are getting the data, but your screen is blank because **Oracle returns all database columns in UPPERCASE** (e.g., VID, CATEGORY_NAME, CREATED_AT), but your React code is still looking for the old camelCase keys (e.g., vid, categoryName, createdAt).
Since it can't find the lowercase keys, it renders empty cells!
We also need to fix your TimePicker at the end of the file so it opens **upwards** and hides past times.
Here are the **two exact replacements** you need to make in **VoucherPosting.js**:
### 1. Fix the Table Data Mapping (To Show the Data)
Find your voucherList.slice(...).map((row) => { block inside the <TableBody> (around line 335) and replace the **entire return ( ... ) block for the row** with this updated version that safely reads the Oracle uppercase keys:
```javascript
