### 2. Fix the TimePicker (Open Upwards & Hide Past Times)
Scroll down to the very bottom of the file (around line 760) where your Step 3 <TimePicker> is located.
Replace your existing <TimePicker> component with this heavily optimized version:
```javascript
                    <TimePicker
                      label="Select Execution Time (Today)"
                      value={scheduledTime}
                      onChange={(newValue) => setScheduledTime(newValue)}
                      disablePast // CRITICAL FIX: Greys out/disables all past AM/PM times
                      minTime={dayjs().add(30, 'minute')}
                      maxTime={dayjs().endOf('day')}
                      timeSteps={{ minutes: 1 }}
                      slotProps={{
                        // CRITICAL FIX: Forces the clock popup to open UPWARDS instead of downwards
                        popper: {
                          placement: "top",
                        },
                        textField: {
                          size: 'small',
                          fullWidth: true,
                          sx: { mb: 3, caretColor: 'transparent' },
                          helperText: "Execution must be scheduled at least 30 mins from now, and before 11:59 PM today.",
                          onKeyDown: (e) => e.preventDefault(),
                          onPaste: (e) => e.preventDefault(),
                          inputProps: { readOnly: true }
                        }
                      }}
                    />

```
Now your rows will render beautifully with the data straight from your Oracle Database, and your time picker will pop up perfectly without letting users select expired times!
